  "about": "The bot match's arena, three lanes (T66, the owner's option 1): a 48 by 32 metre floor, x east and z south, its corner at the origin. Each point has its own lane -- A north, B in the middle, C south -- entered by one door from a rotation corridor behind it. Each spawn room opens into that corridor through two doors offset from the lanes, so no lane sees into a spawn. Two bridges, 2.5 m up, run over the walls between the lanes and flank B; a stair climbs onto each from either end, four steps of half a metre. Every box, platform and stair has its mirror across x = 24, so neither side starts with better ground, and the map is its own mirror across z = 16 too, so A and C are alike. Walls are 5 m, low cover 1.1 m (it hides a crouching bot and lets a standing one shoot over), pillars 2.5 m. A spawn sits in the middle of a one-metre cell, never on its edge, so the walk grid is a mirror as well.",
